    Then each target is http://<service>.<namespace>.svc.<the cluster's DNS domain>:<port>; the render holds that Service with that port; the runner's one egress rule to the namespace names exactly its selector's labels and that container port, 8080 for hello and 8052 for Ascender's web pods; the target's own policy admits the runner there and not the report server, another pod of robot or a pod of another namespace that carries the runner's labels; Ascender's target is checked as the render holds robot-ascender; and without Ascender no rule of robot names it

