    When the CronJob robot-suites, its container's command, arguments and environment, every scheduled job of the render and the monitoring chart's KubeJobFailed are read
    Then robot-suites runs at 45 5 * * * in the cluster's UTC with no time zone of its own, forbids a second run while one runs, starts within 300 seconds or not at all, keeps one successful and three failed jobs, retries no failed pod and ends a run after 1200 seconds, setting no terminationGracePeriodSeconds, so its pod has the default 30 seconds to stop; its pod runs run.sh with the targets as Robot variables, the variables of ks.yaml substituted, and an environment of HOME, KEEP_RUNS and the job's name alone, none of them Robot's; its window, 05:45 to 06:10, overlaps no other CronJob's, base backup's or volume backup's and it runs once a day as the network audit reads a schedule; and the stock KubeJobFailed, a warning of every namespace after 15 minutes, is the alert the docs name for a failed run

