    When the ConfigMaps of the suites and of run.sh, the runner's mounts and each suite's text are read
    Then robot-suites holds common.resource, hello-http.robot and hello-ui.robot and robot-scripts run.sh, byte for byte, by hashed names, and robot-suite-ascender holds ascender-ui.robot under its fixed name, each with Flux's substitution off, mounted read-only and whole at /mnt/robot/suites/base, /mnt/robot/scripts and, optional, /mnt/robot/suites/ascender; each file starts with a comment and each suite imports common.resource; the HTTP suite asks / of hello for a 200 holding hello and /robot-no-such-page for a 404 through Http after opening hello; the UI suite reads hello in the page's body and takes a screenshot; the Ascender suite finds the username and password fields by their labels and the Log In button by its role and name and takes a screenshot; the variables the suites read are the CronJob's; every suite and resource file holds only tab, line feed and printable ASCII in Robot's space-separated format, with no row of the pipe format, and the check of their text as written, a lint and no confinement that follows no escape or variable but in the Http path and the screenshot name, finds no keyword but those listed or defined, no step that types, clicks, presses, uploads or evaluates Python or JavaScript, no assertion operator that evaluates Python spelled out by position and none given by name, no request but a GET of a literal path of the page's own origin, with no variable or escape in it, no screenshot named but by a bare file name, no page but a target's, no chromiumSandbox, no read of the environment, no address with :// and no secret, password, token or cookie outside a comment and the labels it asserts; and no pod reads a Secret

