    Then it asks for the runner's jobs, creates one job robot-run-<UTC time> from cronjob/robot-suites in robot, waits for its pod to leave Pending, follows the job's log and prints it, reads the job's condition and its container's exit code, and exits with that code, printing Every test passed. or 2 tests failed., or the job's reason with status 1 when there is no code, and points at just robot; a broken log says the following stopped, prints none of kubectl's error and reads the result all the same; a failed create names its step and prints none of kubectl's error; and Ctrl-C stops following with status 130, says the job goes on and how to follow it, and deletes nothing

